From: usb-proxy appliance <usb-proxy@local>
Subject: [PATCH] dts: orangepi-zero: bring cpu1 up without PSCI (SPL Falcon boot)

The SPL Falcon boot enters the kernel in secure SVC with no PSCI
monitor, so the "psci" enable-method U-Boot proper used to add is gone
and Linux ran on cpu0 only, which cost the bridge about 20 % of its
throughput (6.1 -> 4.9 MB/s, 2026-10-03).

In secure mode the kernel can drive CPUCFG and PRCM itself. The kernel's
A31 SMP bring-up (reset, L1 reset, the power clamps at PRCM+0x140 and
the power-off gate at PRCM+0x100) is the sequence U-Boot's psci.c uses
on the H3, so hand it the two register blocks under the A31 compatibles
and select it on /cpus. A U-Boot proper boot still puts "psci" on each
cpu node, which the kernel checks first. The PRCM node is disabled so
the A31 PRCM MFD driver does not bind on top of the H3's r_ccu; the SMP
code finds the node by compatible regardless of status. The method has
no cpu_die, so cpu1 can no longer be offlined; power-tune's idle offline
turns into a no-op. Applies after 0009.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [appliance-specific]
Signed-off-by: usb-proxy appliance <usb-proxy@local>
---
--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/allwinner/sun8i-h2-plus-orangepi-zero.dts
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/allwinner/sun8i-h2-plus-orangepi-zero.dts
@@ -279,3 +279,32 @@
 	status = "okay";
 	usb0_id_det-gpios = <&pio 6 12 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>; /* PG12 */
 };
+
+/* usb-proxy appliance: bring cpu1 up without PSCI. The SPL Falcon boot
+ * (U-Boot patch 0003) enters the kernel in secure SVC with no PSCI monitor,
+ * so the PSCI enable-method U-Boot proper used to add is gone and only
+ * cpu0 came up (~20 % less bridge throughput). In secure mode the kernel
+ * can drive CPUCFG and PRCM itself; the A31 bring-up sequence (reset, L1
+ * reset, power clamps at PRCM+0x140, power-off gate at PRCM+0x100) is the
+ * one U-Boot's own psci.c uses on the H3. The method sits on /cpus so a
+ * U-Boot proper boot, which puts enable-method = "psci" on each cpu node,
+ * still wins. The PRCM node is disabled so the A31 PRCM MFD driver stays
+ * away from the H3's r_ccu registers; the SMP code finds it by compatible
+ * regardless of status. No cpu_die in this method: cpu1 cannot be offlined
+ * (power-tune's idle offline becomes a no-op, cpu1 idles in WFI). */
+&{/cpus} {
+	enable-method = "allwinner,sun6i-a31";
+};
+
+&{/soc} {
+	cpucfg@1f01c00 {
+		compatible = "allwinner,sun6i-a31-cpuconfig";
+		reg = <0x01f01c00 0x300>;
+	};
+
+	prcm@1f01400 {
+		compatible = "allwinner,sun6i-a31-prcm";
+		reg = <0x01f01400 0x200>;
+		status = "disabled";
+	};
+};
